jobs.description:
We do have a few wishes before we can offer you this job:
-- You will need to have a C driving license with code 95;
-- You speak and understand Dutch or English well;  
-- You are customer-friendly, flexible and solution-oriented;     
-- You handle fresh food products with care.           

NICE VACANCY FOR A TRUCK DRIVER 

-- EARN MONEY WHILE DRIVING THROUGH THE NETHERLANDS?
-- Yes, that will be possible soon!

-- At a renowned fresh food and catering company, you can pick up the most tasteful culinary dishes and deliver them to various hotels, restaurants, healthcare institutions or simply to festivals and private parties!

-- You travel a lot and therefore work many hours, for which you get paid!
& every day fresh and healthy snacks are ready for you on the go! 

-- We offer you:
-- A good working atmosphere with motivated and experienced colleagues;
-- A comfortable truck;
-- Excellent primary and secondary employment conditions, in accordance with the collective labor agreement;
-- Development opportunities and training.
-------- If you are interested, please let us know!

We are looking for experienced Ground Engineers B1 or B2. Are you up for this great opportunity?

After working hard with your team to deliver a Boeing 787 to your customer in perfect condition, you wave it off with pride. On to the next team challenge: solve a complicated avionic task on the Boeing 777 that has just rolled in! Or a P-inspection at Schiphol Centre while your colleague is doing the Software load. 

Tasks & responsibilities
Ensuring (maintenance) processes on the ground run flawlessly;
Perform inspection, maintenance and modification acitvities and supervise them professionally;
Carry out the work according to the required specifications and in compliance with the various regulations (such as those from the Safety Management System);
Release aircraft to service by means of a Certificate of Release to Service which, in your opinion, are suitable for safe flight operations;
Improve the current maintenance processes structurally and proactively;
Contribute to the further development of your team.

What else will you bring with you?
Demonstrable relevant work experience as (EASA) licensed Ground Engineer for one or more of the following aircraft types B737, B777, A330, A320 NEO and/or B787 (A dossier/document check is part of the selection process);
Good (technical) English, both spoken and written, is a must;
Good Dutch, both spoken and written, is an advantage
Experience working in a team is a plus.

The world is at your feet as a certified engine mechanic. You maintain, overhaul, and modify aircraft engines and individual components. It's also your responsibility to certify them. With your experience, you serve as a role model for junior engine mechanics.

You test the engine for internal damage and detect any anomalies;• You work with various engine types;• You always keep the customer’s requirements in mind;• You report daily to the team lead and the lead mechanic of the Engine Shop;• You perform administrative tasks;• You adhere to safety regulations.

You’ll be part of Engine Services, a division of Engineering & Maintenance (E&M) where you’ll work in the Maintenance, Repair & Overhaul (MRO) department. You will work in shifts: one week of day shifts and one week of evening shifts.

You’re a real techie and love working with your hands. You work quickly but precisely, always spotting potential errors immediately. You also have a strong sense of responsibility and find it important that you and your team can work safely. You don’t hesitate to address colleagues if they don’t follow the regulations. Additionally, you enjoy sharing your experience with junior engine mechanics and helping them find their way in the department.

Furthermore:
You are authorized to perform maintenance on aircraft engines;
You can work independently and sign off on completed work;
You speak and understand (technical) English well;
You have at least three years of experience as an engine mechanic;
You are familiar with engine types CFM56-7B, CF6, GEnx, and LEAP.
